# Same security posture as the repo root: npm resolves per-project config from
# THIS directory (nearest package.json), so the root .npmrc would otherwise be
# silently bypassed here — restate it explicitly.
#
# Electron's binary is fetched by its install script, which this flag blocks by
# design. The binary is NOT needed for typecheck / electron-vite build / unit
# tests — only for actually launching the app (dev / e2e smoke). Fetch it
# explicitly + auditable when needed:  npm run bootstrap:electron
ignore-scripts=true
